  data:  # dbde
    kind: work_item  # dbde
    title: "Reverse slice seed selection: filter by LOC or calls-only out-degree"  # dbde
    status: todo_soft  # dbde
    priority: 3  # dbde
    parent:  # dbde
    tags:  # dbde
    - analysis_quality  # dbde
    before: []  # dbde
    duplicate_of: []  # dbde
    not_duplicate_of: []  # dbde
    pr_ref:  # dbde
    description: "DEEP bakeoff assessment (deep-20260409-054615, prometheus) found that pick_reverse_slice_seeds selects 1-line interface stubs (genericSeriesSet.Err, BucketIterator.Next/At) because dispatches_to edges inflate their out-degree past _MIN_OUT_DEGREE=3. These methods have span 1 line but out-degree 20-41 because every concrete implementation is a dispatches_to edge.\n\nRoot cause: out_degree in pick_reverse_slice_seeds (scripts/bakeoff-deep line ~1026) counts ALL edge types. Interface methods accumulate dispatches_to edges that look like high out-degree but aren't actual function calls.\n\nTwo possible fixes:\n(a) Only count calls-type edges for out_degree in seed selection (most precise).\n(b) Add a minimum LOC check (e.g., skip symbols with end_line - start_line < 3) to filter trivial stubs.\n\nOption (a) is preferred because it addresses the root cause (dispatches_to edges aren't 'calls') rather than using LOC as a proxy."  # dbde
    fields: {}  # dbde
